// endpoint_adopt_host_workspace.proto — AdoptHostWorkspace: Emacs's half of
// the per-workspace handover rendezvous. HOST section, called on the NEW
// daemon's connection after the OLD daemon pushed `transferred` for this
// workspace. The VERB identifies the participant — Emacs and the webview
// have sibling adopt verbs, so no request field self-declares the caller's
// kind.
//
// RENDEZVOUS SEMANTICS: the expected participants are the holders of the
// workspace's WatchHostWorkspace and WatchWebWorkspace streams at the moment
// the old daemon announced the transfer. The new daemon completes adoption
// — claim the workspace's kernel lock, adopt the running shim, drain held
// intake — only when EVERY expected participant has called; all calls then
// succeed together. A workspace with no streams (headless) transfers with
// no rendezvous at all, via WSM facts and the lock alone.

